// Switch component - boolean yes/no question.
// Submitted/stored value is boolean (true/false); state labels are presentation-only (issue #158).
// Display modes:
//  - 'buttons': two radio buttons styled as a button pair; both states are explicit,
//    so an unanswered field submits nothing and 'required' means "pick one".
//    defaultState=true prechecks the ON button; defaultState=false prechecks NOTHING
//    (prechecking OFF would silently pre-answer the question and defeat 'required').
//  - 'toggle': a single styled checkbox; checked submits true, unchecked submits nothing
//    (standard HTML checkbox semantics, same as fmdb:checkbox). 'required' means "must be ON" -
//    use it for acknowledgement-style questions only.
// fmdbmix:booleanField makes the field a conditional-logic source (is true / is false).
// Both display modes expose the state to the generic logic reader: 'toggle' as a lone
// checkbox (checked state), 'buttons' as a radio pair submitting "true"/"false".
[fmdbext:switch] > jnt:content, fmdbmix:element, fmdbmix:profileMappableField, fmdbmix:booleanField, fmdbmix:validationMessages
 - helpText (string, richtext[ckeditor.toolbar='FormidableHelp',ckeditor.customConfig='$context/modules/formidable-engine/javascript/ckeditor/helpTextConfig.js']) i18n indexed=no
 - displayMode (string, choicelist[resourceBundle]) = 'toggle' autocreated indexed=no < 'toggle', 'buttons'
 - onLabel (string) = resourceBundle('fmdbext_switch.defaultOnLabel') autocreated i18n indexed=no
 - offLabel (string) = resourceBundle('fmdbext_switch.defaultOffLabel') autocreated i18n indexed=no
 - defaultState (boolean) = false indexed=no
 - required (boolean) = false
